I vote for silly vitalism. It depends intensely on how EXACTLY
EXACTLY is. Thinking about how cells probably evolved in the first
place, I'd bet that there are many paths to creating cellular life
_de novo_ as long as the copying of nucleic acids is as accurate as
what happens in mitosis.

